            "review_title": "Review at Metta Vegetarian Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Trishka-9\nChapel Hill, North Carolina166 contributions\n0\nBleh! Greasy, fishy-tasting food\nDec 2019\nMenu didn’t appeal to me at all, a lot of fried stuff and mushroom, rice vermicelli dishes. I ordered the brown rice spring rolls, and left half uneaten because they were so greasy and tasted super fishy. The server assured me that it was the seaweed, not fish or fish sauce, but I’ve never had such fishy-tasting seaweed before. So it was fishy on several levels, haha! Staff seemed sulky, and I was seated at the table right in front of where they all hang out, which was uncomfortable. They bring you a tiny “moist towelette” packet when you sit down, which showed up on my bill. Overall one of the most unpleasant meals in recent memory. Extra star for atmosphere, the one nice English-speaking server, and credit cards being accepted.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten January 6, 2020",
